WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.213
How do you turn parametric lines and
planes into x, y, z equations? You can

00:05.213 --> 00:10.427
eliminate a parameter. In this lesson we
write Cartesian equations for lines and

00:10.427 --> 00:15.640
planes. By the end, Write Cartesian
equations for lines and planes.

00:15.640 --> 00:21.220
For a line through x zero y zero with
direction p q, eliminate t to get q times

00:21.220 --> 00:26.800
x minus x zero equals p times y minus y
zero.

00:26.800 --> 00:31.025
With point two one and direction minus one
minus three, the equation becomes minus

00:31.025 --> 00:35.251
three x plus y equals minus five.

00:35.251 --> 00:39.124
For a plane through three points, cross
two direction vectors to get the normal,

00:39.124 --> 00:42.997
then use n dot r equals n dot p.

00:42.997 --> 00:47.319
A common mistake is to leave the parameter
in the final equation. Pause and decide

00:47.319 --> 00:51.640
whether that is right. Eliminate t
completely.

00:51.640 --> 00:57.753
Your turn. Find the Cartesian line through
one two with direction two one. Pause the

00:57.753 --> 01:03.867
video. Hint: Use q times x minus x zero
equals p times y minus y zero.

01:03.867 --> 01:09.287
x minus two y equals minus three. In a new
context, A plane through three points uses

01:09.287 --> 01:14.707
a normal from a cross product. Rate your
confidence from one to five.

01:14.707 --> 01:18.953
Cartesian lines come from eliminating the
parameter, and planes come from a normal

01:18.953 --> 01:23.200
vector. Next, we multiply matrices.
